                <pb facs="0615" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7053</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-20T11:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 20—7:11
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>307. My 297, June 15, 3 p.m. In a further note dated yesterday Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs states that in view of the progress made in the work of clearing
                    the sea and of the clear demarcation of the zone of fighting the commander in
                    chief of the Japanese squadron at Nikolaevsk has decided to make free the
                    navigation of ships in the waters of the [Bay of] de Kastri and the sea north of
                    Dzhaore <pb facs="0616" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/> promontory after June 20th save
                    that strict control will continue to be exercised over arms, ammunition, and
                    other articles of which there is a fear of their being put to the use of the
                    Partisans.</p>
                <p>All consuls informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
